{"name":"Library Card","hex":"#e6c19f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"library card","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A card or document issued by a library to an individual or an organization entitling them or their representatives to borrow materials."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/library_card"}],"entries":[{"title":"Library card","blocks":[{"text":"A library card is part of an integrated library system which can refer to several cards traditionally used for the management of books and patrons in a library. In its most common use, a library card serves similar functions as a corporate membership card. A person who holds a library card has borrowing or other privileges associated with the issuing library. Library cards can grant the user much more than books such as museum admission, game controllers, DVDs and other media."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/ROC_National_Central_Library_membership_card_20050531_face.jpg/330px-ROC_National_Central_Library_membership_card_20050531_face.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Library_card","wikidata":"Q2367654"},{"title":"Library","blocks":[{"text":"A library is a collection of books, and possibly other materials and media, that is accessible for use by its members and members of allied institutions. Libraries provide physical or digital materials, and may be a physical location, a virtual space, or both. A library's collection normally includes printed materials which can be borrowed, and usually also includes a reference section of publications which may only be utilized inside the premises. Resources such as commercial releases of films, television programmes, other video recordings, radio, music and audio recordings may be available in many formats. These include DVDs, Blu-rays, CDs, cassettes, or other applicable formats such as microform. They may also provide access to information, music or other content held on bibliographic databases. In addition, some libraries offer creation stations for makers which offer access to a 3D printing station with a 3D scanner."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/SanDiegoCityCollegeLearningResource_-_bookshelf.jpg/330px-SanDiegoCityCollegeLearningResource_-_bookshelf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Library","wikidata":"Q7075"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Library_card.jpg/330px-Library_card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Library_card.jpg/330px-Library_card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An example of a borrowing card, formerly in common use to track books","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALibrary_card.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Library_of_Ashurbanipal.jpg/500px-Library_of_Ashurbanipal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Library_of_Ashurbanipal.jpg/1280px-Library_of_Ashurbanipal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Library_of_Ashurbanipal.jpg/500px-Library_of_Ashurbanipal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Library of Ashurbanipal in Mesopotamia, c. 1500–539 BC.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALibrary_of_Ashurbanipal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Videos_in_boxes_in_Monmouth_County_Library_eastern_branch.JPG/500px-Videos_in_boxes_in_Monmouth_County_Library_eastern_branch.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_